---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";
import { visitIdsForArticle } from "../../data/catalog";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "alternatives")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
const description =
  "DataFast, Google Analytics, Amplitude, PostHog, Mixpanel, Plausible, and Fathom alternatives, compared by the job a founder actually needs done.";
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics alternatives"
  description={description}
  kicker="Alternatives"
  lede="Each guide below compares several tools. DataFast is the pick when you need revenue attribution. It is not the pick when you need a product-analytics suite."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Alternatives" }]}
>
  <p>An “alternative” is only useful if you name the job you are leaving. Founders usually mean one of three jobs: a lighter report than GA4, a privacy-first traffic script, or a product suite that can replace Amplitude, Mixpanel, or PostHog. Those are different shortlists.</p>
  <p>DataFast belongs on the first and second lists when the question is which channel or page brought a payment. PostHog, Mixpanel, and Amplitude belong on the third list. Plausible and Fathom belong on the privacy-first traffic list, with revenue features that are real but not the whole product. The guides below keep those lines visible. Public prices are as of 24 November 2026.</p>
  <p>If the tool you have today is DataFast, start with the <a href="/alternatives/datafast/">DataFast alternatives</a>. That page covers when to stay, then links the six <a href="/compare/">DataFast comparisons</a> and the <a href="/pricing/datafast/">pricing ladder</a>. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> is the product itself. The <a href="/compare/posthog-vs-google-analytics/">PostHog vs GA4 comparison</a> sits next to these pages on purpose.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Guides in this section</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
          visits: visitIdsForArticle(article.id),
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
